---
import { CIPHER_ACTION_TEXT, DECIPHER_ACTION_TEXT } from "../constants/text";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="User Manual">
	<main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 flex-col justify-center px-6 py-16 text-left">
		<h1 class="mb-8 text-center text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">User Manual</h1>

		<div class="space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
			<section class="space-y-3">
				<p>
					Welcome to this demo of Caesar Cipher algorithm. This tool lets you encrypt or decrypt any message using the
					classic Caesar cipher. It works by shifting each letter of your text a fixed number of
					steps along the alphabet.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-100">How to use it</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">
					<li>
						Choose an <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Action</strong>. Click{" "}
						<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">{CIPHER_ACTION_TEXT}</strong> to hide a message or{" "}
						<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">{DECIPHER_ACTION_TEXT}</strong> to reveal one that was
						ciphered before.
					</li>
					<li>
						Pick a <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Vocabulary</strong>. Use{" "}
						<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">English</strong> or{" "}
						<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Spanish</strong>. The Spanish alphabet
						includes the letter <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">&ntilde;</strong>, so
						words with &ntilde; are handled correctly.
					</li>
					<li>
						Write your message in the <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Text to{" "}
						{CIPHER_ACTION_TEXT.toLowerCase()}</strong> field.
					</li>
					<li>
						Set the <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Shift</strong> value between{" "}
						<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">3</strong> and{" "}
						<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">7</strong>. This is the number of steps
						each letter will move.
					</li>
					<li>
						Press the <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">{CIPHER_ACTION_TEXT}</strong> button. The
						button label changes to <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">{DECIPHER_ACTION_TEXT}</strong>{" "}
						when Decrypt mode is active.
					</li>
					<li>
						The result will appear in the textbox below.
					</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-100">A quick example</h2>
				<p>
					With <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">{CIPHER_ACTION_TEXT}</strong> mode, the{" "}
					<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">English</strong> vocabulary and a shift of{" "}
					<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">3</strong>, typing{" "}
					<span class="text-slate-100">hello</span> produces{" "}
					<span class="text-slate-100">khoor</span>. Switch to{" "}
					<strong class="font-semibold text-slate-100">{DECIPHER_ACTION_TEXT}</strong> mode, type{" "}
					<span class="text-slate-100">khoor</span> with the same shift, and you get{" "}
					<span class="text-slate-100">hello</span> back.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="space-y-3">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-100">Things to keep in mind</h2>
				<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
					<li>
						Characters that are not letters (spaces, numbers, punctuation) are kept unchanged.
					</li>
					<li>
						Uppercase and lowercase letters are preserved after ciphering.
					</li>
					<li>
						The same shift value must be used to encrypt and then decrypt a message, otherwise the
						result will not match the original.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</div>

		<a
			href="/"
			class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-500 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-indigo-400 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-indigo-300"
		>
			Go to main page
		</a>
	</main>
</Layout>